    "description": "An Order Service commits a new purchase and then announces that fact to several independently deployed systems. The Billing Service charges the customer, the Search Projector refreshes its catalog, the Loyalty Service awards points, and an Audit Service stores the record. None of these consumers may depend on another consumer, and adding a new consumer must not require the Order Service to change. The announcement has no intended recipient and requires no response; delivery may occur more than once, so each record carries a stable event identity and occurrence time. A consumer may reject an unknown future record kind without causing the producer to wait or retry against it. The design must clearly distinguish an immutable statement about a completed change from an instruction addressed to a particular worker, while preserving enough metadata for broker-side subscription filtering.",
    "decision_statement": "Choose one-way, recipient-independent publication for a completed order change, with no required response and no producer coupling to downstream consumers.",
    "notes": "event-message primary: one-way recipient-independent publication of a completed change with no required response; document-message and message are the record and envelope near-misses; property-based-serializer supports broker-side filtering metadata."
  },
